PI text; it is excluded. The 120 blocks are comment/docstring edits with normalized executable AST and directive text unchanged; 135 changed docstrings across both leaves are strictly shorter. docs/env-vars.md updates only 5 config.py line references shifted by prose shortening. Root focused suite: 1189 passed, 7 skipped, with 2 initial public-surface failures; both exact failures and both generators pass after the correction. Full make verify is running. Independent per-block review is pending.","timestamp":1792751257324444101}],"created_at":1788570640563265637,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"9a0c69c0-449f-4b65-897c-f89148d53e6d","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"d97a-89e3-c778-4ebf"},{"link_uuid":"8c15a4b1-57d9-4cca-b19b-dc4ce77a1393","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"a3b2-22f7-60c5-4e44"},{"link_uuid":"3386bf34-e73c-4216-9442-234d2015dd38","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"8239-984d-00ef-47df"},{"link_uuid":"47fa224d-ef62-4424-b69a-bcdaf036a659","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"ca98-0c64-502a-4997"},{"link_uuid":"993b66f9-561c-4ba1-aeac-f54700dbc669","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"16bf-a8d8-ca71-42d9"},{"link_uuid":"fab83062-a98e-4f03-8dfa-b9810b5400dd","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"10cc-11db-239e-42c2"},{"link_uuid":"712a2e2a-78c2-478e-9351-5f635cb79962","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"ab0b-f692-5d78-46cd"},{"link_uuid":"866eea6a-f828-49db-a0ca-b58c0f27b92e","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"a921-a224-c618-414d"},{"link_uuid":"f5e1c4c0-b6f8-4ae5-93d5-ac8a033d3f86","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"24c0-3ed5-fa97-4610"},{"link_uuid":"c1857459-2940-4377-95e3-34a83dbaca58","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"b78f-4db0-ff09-4c88"},{"link_uuid":"a44a1825-454d-49f2-9615-943458726dfb","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"5d50-5480-0b6a-4394"}],"description":"## Context / immutable audit base\nAt `7840899ea7ac0609bf3e0dec5e26effdbda1ec6c`, the 12 files below contain 120 confirmed prose blocks that can be shortened without executable change. The legacy plan cited broad ranges from an older tree and mixed prose with code, concise/load-bearing text, and directives. The worktree started at this immutable base. Listed spans are historical audit citations at d6669496cae441fc8381b5ee6de21a3993defd84, never edit coordinates. The independent review cites each surviving before block at 7840899ea7ac0609bf3e0dec5e26effdbda1ec6c.\n\n## Exact prose allowlist\nPaths below are relative to `src/rebar/`. Stable IDs are `path::D:<qualified-owner>@<base-span>` for Python docstrings, `path::C:<qualified-owner>@<base-span>` for Python comments, and `path::J/Y@<base-span>` for JS/YAML comments. Only the 120 surviving blocks listed below may change. ADR 0119 moved or removed 13 original audit blocks before this worktree started: 12 from _mcp_writes.py and 1 from mcp_server.py. Four moved prose blocks now live in _mcp_derive.py; removed tool descriptions are runtime strings and are excluded. The surviving _mcp_writes.run_workflow docstring is also excluded because FastMCP publishes it as the tool description; changing it fails the public tool golden and generated reference checks.\n\n- _mcp_serving.py (5): D:module@1-18, D:make_sigterm_handler@67-83, D:run_http_with_grace@107-129, D:run_mcp@175-181, C:run_mcp@191-194.\n- _mcp_writes.py (3): D:module@1-16, D:register_write_tools@21-30, C:register_write_tools.run_workflow._bg@87-90.\n- _mcp_derive.py (4): D:cross_session_warning@127-131, D:push_status@140-144, D:ack@160-162, D:attach_warning@192-194. These 4 are relocated commentary from the former _mcp_writes.py helper surface.\n- _opcert_signing.py (15): D:module@1-13, D:OpcertKeyUnavailable@44-48, D:_derive_opcert_pub@63-69, D:_generate_opcert_key@100-108, D:ensure_opcert_key@165-181, D:opcert_principal@215-221, D:_opcert_own_key_paths@241-248, D:_ssh_pub_body@275-278, D:_warn_if_verify_cannot_resolve@298-306, D:_pinned_public_key_bodies@329-356, D:_refuse_if_pinned_principal_key_mismatch@382-402, D:mint_opcert_record@435-444, D:sign_opcert_manifest@514-522, C:module@36-39, C:_derive_opcert_pub@79-84.\n- _opcert_verify.py (10): D:module@1-13, D:_opcert_subject_binding_error@25-43, D:_required_environment@101-110, D:_opcert_trust_root@137-148, D:verify_opcert_record@170-207, C:verify_opcert_record@241-244, C:verify_opcert_record@247-253, C:verify_opcert_record@255-258, C:verify_opcert_record@260-264, C:verify_opcert_record@326-329.\n- _operation_config.py (12): D:module@1-29, D:_source_kinds@54-65, D:_validate_jsonish@82-87, D:OperationSnapshot@113-118, D:OperationSnapshot.build@134-139, D:compose_operation_snapshot@208-215, D:active_snapshot@244-249, D:bind_operation_snapshot@255-260, D:compose_and_bind_operation_snapshot@274-291, D:bind_operation_snapshot_for_tools@314-326, C:module@230-237, C:compose_and_bind_operation_snapshot@299-304.\n- _proc.py (5): D:module@1-26, D:reap_process_group@46-61, D:store_repo_root@113-131, D:detached_child_cwd@137-163, D:spawn_detached@195-223.\n- config.py (32): D:plan_review_docs_url@119-123, D:_bound_snapshot_for_root@139-145, D:tracker_dir@167-184, D:tickets_branch@210-221, D:tickets_remote@226-239, D:reset_config_cache@315-318, D:_ordered_layers@336-341, D:_env_signature@363-366, D:_config_probe_paths@416-424, D:_resolve@445-448, D:load_config@472-487, D:mcp_readonly@523-533, D:mcp_gate@545-555, D:compose_config@567-573, D:_git_toplevel_of_cwd@600-606, D:reconciler_repo_root@623-640, D:resolve_jira_detection@673-683, D:resolve_push_mode@698-706, D:read_secret_env@716-721, D:read_config_file@726-730, D:read_reserved_section@740-748, D:cli_overrides_for@766-769, D:resolve_with_sources@777-785, C:module@13-15, C:module@38-42, C:module@91-96, C:module@108-114, C:tracker_dir@196-202, C:module@251-270, C:module@273-283, C:load_config@488-492, C:load_config@496-499.\n- mcp_server.py (11): 3 surviving docstrings and 8 comments from the historical audit list below, excluding deleted C:module@359-366: D:_mcp_gate@382-388, D:_resolve_http_runtime@426-436, D:compose_startup_opcert_binding@644-661, C:module@55-66, C:_readonly@393-397, C:build_server@511-515, C:build_server@545-559, C:build_server@567-573, C:build_server@611-623, C:main@676-679, C:main@711-713.\n- mirror_guard.py (3): D:replication_verdict@58-65, D:ruleset_verdict@85-91, D:_replication_check_with_lag_tolerance@204-210.\n- secret_screen.py (9): D:module@1-34, D:SecretFinding@121-126, D:iter_line_matches@148-153, D:_safe_segment@179-186, D:screen_event_data@194-201, D:override_record@218-223, C:module@53-55, C:module@58-72, C:module@92-100.\n- signing.py (11): D:module@1-22, D:verify_attestation_record@127-145, D:_sign_manifest_under_lock@171-176, D:_resolve_and_reduce@247-252, D:most_recent_attestation@282-291, D:_record_for_kind@301-305, D:verify_signature@313-324, D:verify_attestations@336-339, D:verify_signature_cli@395-405, C:module@69-73, C:module@111-114.\n\n## Contracts, consumers, and exclusions\nPreserve MCP drain order and handshake; FastMCP tool names, schemas, force/gate semantics, and delivery fields; race-safe op-cert key custody, environment/principal binding, trust order, signed-subject replay defense, and authenticated material; immutable operation snapshots; process-group reaping and durable detached cwd; config exports/precedence/cache/tombstones; HTTP auth/stateless/proxy behavior; refuse-not-redact secret screening; and legacy/new signing dispatch. FastMCP consumes registered tool docstrings. The mcp_server module docstring is excluded because facade tests require its in-process-read statement; mirror_guard's module docstring is excluded because argparse publishes it.\n\nConcise/load-bearing source prose outside the allowlist stays byte-identical. So do runtime strings, assertions, fixtures, decorators, subprocess arguments, config values, and all directive/shebang physical lines. The only non-Python change is generated docs/env-vars.md: 5 config.py source-line references shifted by this comment shortening; environment keys and behavior remain unchanged.\n\n## Verification and independent review\nParse base and final Python with `type_comments=True`; replace only allowlisted leading owner docstrings, normalize only `ast.TypeIgnore.lineno`, and require the remaining AST/runtime tree to match. A zero-context base-to-final hunk guard and independent block receipts restrict every change to the surviving allowlist at 7840899ea7ac0609bf3e0dec5e26effdbda1ec6c. Run all six structured DD commands, including exact one-commit paths, focused consumers, scoped diff integrity, hygiene, and untimed worktree-venv `make verify`.\n\nA reviewer who did not author the patch records a leaf-linked TSV with exactly 120 PASS rows, one per stable ID: `stable_id,before_citation,final_citation,preserved_contract_or_consumer,directives_exact,before_words,final_words,reviewer_session,semantic_pass,bloat_pass`. Every `final_words` is smaller; missing, extra, duplicate, or FAIL rows block closure.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Exactly 120 allowlisted blocks have smaller final word counts.\n- [ ] Non-allowlisted prose and all directive/shebang lines remain exact.\n- [ ] The immutable-base runtime/non-comment oracle passes for every owned file.\n- [ ] Every preserved contract or consumer has an independent TSV PASS citation.\n- [ ] HEAD^..HEAD changes exactly the 12 source paths plus generated docs/env-vars.md and focused, diff-integrity, and hygiene checks exit 0.\n- [ ] Untimed worktree-venv `make verify` exits 0.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_serving.py","reason":"Condense 5 graceful-serving comment blocks."},{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py","reason":"Condense 3 non-published write-tool prose blocks; preserve the run_workflow tool description byte-for-byte."},{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_derive.py","reason":"Condense 4 relocated helper docstrings after ADR 0119."},{"path":"src/rebar/_opcert_signing.py","reason":"Condense 15 key custody and minting comment blocks."},{"path":"src/rebar/_opcert_verify.py","reason":"Condense 10 trust, material, and replay comment blocks."},{"path":"src/rebar/_operation_config.py","reason":"Condense 12 snapshot and binding comment blocks."},{"path":"src/rebar/_proc.py","reason":"Condense 5 process lifecycle comment blocks."},{"path":"src/rebar/config.py","reason":"Condense 32 config and resolver comment blocks."},{"path":"src/rebar/mcp_server.py","reason":"Condense 11 surviving transport and registration comment blocks."},{"path":"src/rebar/mirror_guard.py","reason":"Condense 3 verdict and resampling docstrings."},{"path":"src/rebar/secret_screen.py","reason":"Condense 9 detection and safe-reporting comment blocks."},{"path":"src/rebar/signing.py","reason":"Condense 11 dispatch, selection, and CLI comment blocks."},{"path":"docs/env-vars.md","reason":"Regenerate only 5 config.py source-line references shifted by comment shortening; environment keys and runtime behavior are unchanged."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["parent","d6eb-1c6c-88c3-48f6"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"d6eb-1c6c-88c3-48f6","parent_status_uuid":"14b687a2-5d3a-4094-ba2f-fec05b075669","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":["rebar"],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["comments","documentation","maintainability","grouped-remediation"],"ticket_id":"e95f-b385-d913-4c92","ticket_type":"task","title":"Condense comments in src/rebar — cohort 03: mcp_serving–signing","verify_commands":[{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python - <<'PY'\nimport ast, io, subprocess, tokenize\nfrom pathlib import Path\nBASE=\"7840899ea7ac0609bf3e0dec5e26effdbda1ec6c\"\nPATHS=[\"src/rebar/_store/push_state.py\",\"src/rebar/_store/push.py\",\"src/rebar/_store/s3_doctor.py\",\"src/rebar/_store/staging.py\",\"src/rebar/_store/stamped_lock.py\",\"src/rebar/_store/store_usability.py\",\"src/rebar/_store/sync.py\",\"src/rebar/_mcp_serving.py\",\"src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py\",\"src/rebar/_mcp_derive.py\",\"src/rebar/_opcert_signing.py\",\"src/rebar/_opcert_verify.py\",\"src/rebar/_operation_config.py\",\"src/rebar/_proc.py\",\"src/rebar/config.py\",\"src/rebar/mcp_server.py\",\"src/rebar/mirror_guard.py\",\"src/rebar/secret_screen.py\",\"src/rebar/signing.py\"]\ndef normalized(src):\n tree=ast.parse(src,type_comments=True)\n for node in ast.walk(tree):\n  if isinstance(node,ast.TypeIgnore): node.lineno=0\n  body=getattr(node,'body',None)\n  if isinstance(body,list) and body and isinstance(body[0],ast.Expr) and isinstance(body[0].value,ast.Constant) and isinstance(body[0].value.value,str): body[0].value.value='DOCSTRING'\n return ast.dump(tree,include_attributes=False)\ndef directives(src):\n out=[]\n for tok in tokenize.generate_tokens(io.StringIO(src).readline):\n  if tok.type==tokenize.COMMENT and any(s in tok.string for s in ('noqa','type:','pyright:','mypy:','ruff:','fmt:','isort:','pragma:','nosec','coverage:','mechanism-ok:','raw-git-ok:','tickets-boundary-ok:','read-via:','repo-root-ok:')): out.append(tok.string)\n return out\nfor path in PATHS:\n before=subprocess.check_output(['git','show',BASE+':'+path],text=True)\n final=Path(path).read_text(encoding='utf-8')\n assert normalized(before)==normalized(final),('AST/runtime drift',path)\n assert directives(before)==directives(final),('directive drift',path)\nprint('prose-only AST and directive oracle passed for',len(PATHS),'files')\nPY","dd_id":"immutable-prose-only","dd_text":"Grouped commit preserves normalized executable Python AST and physical directive comments against immutable worktree base; independent block receipts enforce the exact prose allowlist."},{"command":"python - <<'PY'\nimport subprocess\nexpected=set([\"src/rebar/_store/push_state.py\",\"src/rebar/_store/push.py\",\"src/rebar/_store/s3_doctor.py\",\"src/rebar/_store/staging.py\",\"src/rebar/_store/stamped_lock.py\",\"src/rebar/_store/store_usability.py\",\"src/rebar/_store/sync.py\",\"src/rebar/_mcp_serving.py\",\"src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py\",\"src/rebar/_mcp_derive.py\",\"src/rebar/_opcert_signing.py\",\"src/rebar/_opcert_verify.py\",\"src/rebar/_operation_config.py\",\"src/rebar/_proc.py\",\"src/rebar/config.py\",\"src/rebar/mcp_server.py\",\"src/rebar/mirror_guard.py\",\"src/rebar/secret_screen.py\",\"src/rebar/signing.py\",\"docs/env-vars.md\"])\nactual=set(subprocess.check_output(['git','diff','--name-only','HEAD^..HEAD'],text=True).splitlines())\nassert actual==expected,{'expected':sorted(expected),'actual':sorted(actual)}\nPY","dd_id":"exact-leaf-paths","dd_text":"The grouped commit changes exactly 20 declared paths: 19 Python source paths plus the generated environment registry."},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py","dd_id":"comment-hygiene","dd_text":"Repository comment hygiene passes."},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" PYPANDOC_PANDOC=/Users/joeoakhart/.local/pandoc-3.9/pandoc-3.9-arm64/bin/pandoc python -m pytest -q tests/unit/test_mcp*.py tests/unit/test_opcert*.py tests/unit/test_*signing*.py tests/unit/test_secret_screen_e7a9.py tests/unit/test_config*.py tests/unit/test_operation_config_source_kinds.py tests/unit/test_mirror_guard.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp*.py tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_attested_signing.py","dd_id":"focused-contracts","dd_text":"Focused subsystem and consumer tests pass."},{"command":"git diff --check HEAD^..HEAD","dd_id":"diff-integrity","dd_text":"The grouped commit contains no whitespace errors."},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" PYPANDOC_PANDOC=/Users/joeoakhart/.local/pandoc-3.9/pandoc-3.9-arm64/bin/pandoc make verify","dd_id":"repository-gates","dd_text":"The untimed complete local CI contract passes with the worktree virtualenv and installed Pandoc 3.9."}]},"source_event_uuids":["4edcae8f-1a13-4e61-8ec4-3bc9a9791786","2e220800-1452